This repository is a focused release for reproducing supersample
retraining experiments on CelebA with ViT, plus related Flights200K
bound experiments.

Substantial infrastructure (dataset loading, ViT wrapper, multicalibration
bin/group utilities, and related helpers) is adapted from the public
empirical multicalibration codebase of Hansen et al.:

  https://github.com/dutchhansen/multicalibration

Paper: When is Multicalibration Post-Processing Necessary?
  https://arxiv.org/abs/2406.06487

That upstream project is released under the MIT License. The original
LICENSE file is retained in this repository. This release uses the
upstream code as implementation infrastructure and does not rely on it
as a source of theoretical claims.
